    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a1">

                <pb facs="0265" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg177"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 329.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Miller to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Adrian, Mich.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I respectfully call attention to the
                    accompanying papers: <list>
                        <item>No. 1. A notice from the imperial court at Bischweiler, Alsace,
                            Germany.</item>
                        <item>No. 2. Affidavit by Charles E. Heintzman.</item>
                        <item>No. 3. Affidavit by Mrs. Frederika Ellegat.</item>
                        <item>No. 4. Certificate of naturalization of Charles E. Heintzman as a
                            citizen of Michigan and of the United States.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The notice in suhstance orders him to report for military duty in the German army
                    in fifty days from date of the citation or that his inheritance from his
                    grandfather will he mulcted 600 marks. He respectfully requests the intervention
                    of the State Department of the United States to protect him in his rights as a
                    citizen of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. R. Miller</hi></signed>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">for Mr. Charles E. Heintzman.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
